const notes = "<p>Fort Lauderdale is built around waterways: the New River, canals and the Intracoastal. Waterfront lots often have limited access, seawalls and docks, so crews may have to lower pieces by hand or use a boat-side approach. Tell the professional about access and what stands near the tree.</p><p>High groundwater and heavy summer rain loosen root systems, and salt air stresses trees close to the beach. Palms are everywhere, and mature oaks and mahogany shade older streets.</p>";

